course: dictionary
lesson: 11437
title: Addicted: when you cannot stop
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Addicted means not able to stop doing or taking something, even when you want to. Some harmful things, such as tobacco, alcohol and some drugs, can make a person's body and mind need them. «Mia's uncle became addicted to tobacco, and he found it very hard to stop.» The clue is found it very hard to stop: he could not just stop when he chose.
explain: Addicted can also mean not able to stop doing something that causes harm, such as playing games for hours. «Some people get addicted to games and keep playing even when they feel tired and grumpy.» Here the clue is keep playing even when they feel tired.
explain: People often use addicted in a light, friendly way too. «I'm addicted to this song!» means Mia likes the song very much and keeps playing it. No one is ill; she just loves it. Check your meaning: if you swap in very much liking, does the sentence still make sense? Yes, so you have understood it.
fact: Addicted means not able to stop taking or doing something, even when you want to.
fact: Harmful things like tobacco, alcohol and some drugs can make people addicted.
fact: Addiction is an illness, and people can get help for it from doctors and other grown-ups.
fact: In everyday talk, «I'm addicted to this song!» means you like something very much.
fact: Common phrases are «addicted to», «become addicted» and «get addicted».
exercise: «Mia's uncle became addicted to tobacco, and he found it very hard to stop.» What does addicted mean here? | Happy to be asked to a party | Keen to learn new songs | *Not able to stop, because his body and mind need it | Very tired after a long walk
exercise: Mia says, «I'm addicted to this song!» What does she mean? | *She likes it very much and listens to it all the time | She is ill and needs a doctor | She has to sing it at school every day | She hates the song
exercise: Which phrase uses addicted correctly? | addicted the door | *become addicted | addicted under the table | addicted my brother
test: Ella says, «Some drugs can make people addicted.» Why is this serious? | The person will feel happy and never tired | *The person may need the drug and find it very hard to stop | It means the drug is always safe | It means the drug is a fun game
test: Which statement about addiction is true? | It goes away if you ignore it | *It is an illness, and people can get help for it | It is only a silly word for liking a snack | It is a kind of sport
exam: In «I'm addicted to this song!», addicted means: | Not able to stop taking a harmful drug | Very hungry | Sleepy after a long day | *Liking something very much
